  "notable_quotes": [
    "MOF separations often face a capacity-selectivity trade-off; narrow-pore size sieving can limit uptake, and prior Zr-TATAB, NEM-7-Cu, and FMF-202a showed this mismatch.",
    "High C3H6 affinity is attributed to exposed metal sites plus uncoordinated tetrazolate N and carboxylate groups that create more accessible C3H6 binding sites.",
    "Mn-dtzip adsorbs much more C3H6 than C2H4 at 100 kPa: 259.1 vs 138.7 cm3 g-1 and 216.4 vs 76.7 cm3 g-1 at two tested temperatures."
  ],
